{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Wannabe Knight","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/wannabe-knight.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/wannabe-knight.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Wannabe Knight","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":10,"temp":0,"max":10,"details":""},"ac":{"value":33,"details":"35 with shield raised"},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"can't speak"},"level":{"value":13},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Wannabe knights appear as regal knights clad in shining armor with a lance at their side. However, upon closer inspection, it has glistening black ooze creeping out of its armor. More jarring yet is the knight's \"steed,\" which is composed of nothing more than the same black ooze that makes up its body.</p>\n<p>Wannabe knights are huge fans of tales of knights and chivalry, so they try to stick to the code that the knights of legend supposedly follow. Acting like a silent knight out of a storybook, wannabe knights value a fair fight and accept the challenge of battle to prove their skill. Far too often, a wannabe's need for glory leads it to attack the actual heroes it encounters. Other times, a wannabe knight might pledge its sword to an entity that convinces it to serve and protect an area.</p>\n<h2>My Kingdom For A Horse</h2>\n<p>Some equipment goes further for wannabe knights than others. Knights welcome new armor but find their own pseudopods to be sufficient weaponry. Their greatest desire is a real horse, which frees their form to create longer weapons and extend their reach. The horse becomes the knight's best friend, receiving doting care. Losing the steed is devastating, though, and many veteran wannabe knights never seek out a replacement as the pain of losing their original mount is simply too great to experience again.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 375/840/1,560 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Lore [Legend], Society)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (positive), fortification, spiked, strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Justin Cando","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":1},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":23,"senses":[{"type":"motion-sense","acuity":"imprecise","range":240}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":26,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":23,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":20,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{},"traits":{"value":["lawful","ooze"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/wannabe-knight.webp","items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/equipment/shields/specific-shields/sturdy-shield.webp","name":"Sturdy Shield (Lesser)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>With a superior design and excellent craftsmanship, this steel shield has higher Hardness than its non-magical counterparts, making it harder to break and destroy.</p>\n<p>The shield has Hardness 10, HP 80, and BT 40.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"sturdy-shield-lesser","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["magical"],"rarity":"common","integrated":null},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"steel-shield","bulk":{"value":1},"hp":{"value":80,"max":80},"hardness":10,"price":{"value":{"gp":360}},"equipped":{"carryType":"held","invested":null,"handsHeld":1},"containerId":null,"size":"med","material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"","img":"","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"acBonus":2,"grade":null,"runes":{"reinforcing":0,"potency":0,"resilient":0,"property":[]},"specific":{"material":{"type":null,"grade":null},"runes":{"reinforcing":0},"integrated":null},"speedPenalty":0,"subitems":[]},"type":"shield","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"CIWVguTLismR00HG":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":168888012268